#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git 2.42.1 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:8
msgid ""
"There is nothing exciting to see here.  Relative to Git 2.42, this release "
"contains the fixes that have already been merged to the 'master' branch of "
"the development towards Git 2.43 that has been tagged as Git 2.43.0-rc0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since Git 2.42.0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:13
msgid "Tests that are known to pass with LSan are now marked as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:16
msgid ""
"Flaky \"git p4\" tests, as well as \"git svn\" tests, are now skipped in the "
"(rather expensive) sanitizer CI job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:20
msgid ""
"Tests with LSan from time to time seem to emit harmless message that makes "
"our tests unnecessarily flaky; we work it around by filtering the "
"uninteresting output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:22
msgid "GitHub CI workflow has learned to trigger Coverity check."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:25
msgid ""
"Overly long label names used in the sequencer machinery are now chopped to "
"fit under filesystem limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:27
msgid "Scalar updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:31
msgid ""
"Tweak GitHub Actions CI so that pushing the same commit to multiple branch "
"tips at the same time will not waste building and testing the same thing "
"twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:34
msgid ""
"The commit-graph verification code that detects mixture of zero and non-zero "
"generation numbers has been updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:37
msgid ""
"\"git diff -w --exit-code\" with various options did not work correctly, "
"which is being addressed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:40
msgid ""
"transfer.unpackLimit ought to be used as a fallback, but overrode fetch."
"unpackLimit and receive.unpackLimit instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:43
msgid ""
"The use of API between two calls to require_clean_work_tree() from the "
"sequencer code has been cleaned up for consistency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:46
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-such-option\" and other corner cases around the exit status "
"of the \"diff\" command has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:49
msgid ""
"\"git for-each-ref --sort='contents:size'\" sorts the refs according to size "
"numerically, giving a ref that points at a blob twelve-byte"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:50
msgid "long before showing a blob hundred-byte (100) long."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:53
msgid ""
"Various fixes to the behavior of \"rebase -i\" when the command got "
"interrupted by conflicting changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:56
msgid ""
"References from description of the `--patch` option in various manual pages "
"have been simplified and improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:59
msgid ""
"\"git grep -e A --no-or -e B\" is accepted, even though the negation of "
"\"or\" did not mean anything, which has been tightened."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:63
msgid ""
"The completion script (in contrib/) has been taught to treat the \"-t\" "
"option to \"git checkout\" and \"git switch\" just like the \"--track\" "
"option, to complete remote-tracking branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:66
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index -R <(one) <(two)\" did not work correctly, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:69
msgid ""
"Update \"git maintenance\" timers' implementation based on systemd timers to "
"work with WSL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:73
msgid ""
"\"git diff --cached\" codepath did not fill the necessary stat information "
"for a file when fsmonitor knows it is clean and ended up behaving as if it "
"is not clean, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:77
msgid ""
"Clarify how \"alias.foo = : git cmd ; aliased-command-string\" should be "
"spelled with necessary whitespaces around punctuation marks to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:81
msgid ""
"HTTP Header redaction code has been adjusted for a newer version of cURL "
"library that shows its traces differently from earlier versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:84
msgid ""
"An error message given by \"git send-email\" when given a malformed address "
"did not give correct information, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:87
msgid ""
"UBSan options were not propagated through the test framework to git run via "
"the httpd, unlike ASan options, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.1.txt:88
msgid ""
"Also contains various documentation updates, code clean-ups and minor fixups."
msgstr ""
